## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a complete edge-CV pipeline: real-time monocular 3D pose with per-object velocity, occlusion robustness, and rapid on-device adaptation to unseen parts. Emphasizes practical data strategies and evaluation in an industrial setting.

## Key Concepts
- Real-time monocular 3D pose estimation
- Per-instance velocity prediction for planning
- On-device few-shot adaptation (5-shot)
- Occlusion handling and data fusion strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: forward pass with adaptation trigger
function forward(frame, exemplars){
  let features = backbone(frame);
  let detections = detector(features);
  let poses = poseHead(features, detections);
  let vel = velocityHead(features, detections, previous);
  if (exemplars) adapt(poses, exemplars);
  return {detections, poses, vel};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you quantify robustness to occlusion in your evaluation?
- What ablation would you run to isolate the velocity head contribution?
